During the ESLint analysis, two security and performance issues were found in the file services/fileService.js:

Use of readFileSync with a non-literal filename

The code uses fs.readFileSync() with a dynamic (non-literal) file path.

This creates a risk of Path Traversal attacks, where an attacker could manipulate the input path to access sensitive system files.

Detected by rule: security/detect-non-literal-fs-filename.

Use of synchronous file system method

readFileSync blocks the Node.js event loop.

This can negatively impact application performance and cause delays for other requests, especially in concurrent environments.

Detected by rule: node/no-sync.

These vulnerabilities are important to address by using asynchronous file operations and validating file paths before reading files.